=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
No fault exists in this network. The helpdesk ticket's assertion that the WAN
uplink carrying traffic toward 128.168.0.0/16 is down is incorrect. Direct
testing from every implicated segment — Office LAN (office_pc, enquiry),
Principle LAN (pc0, laptop0) — to multiple Internet Lab hosts (pc2 at
128.168.0.2, pc3 at 128.168.0.3, pc4 at 128.168.0.4) produces 0% packet loss
at normal latency (~1–2 ms). Both physical WAN links that could carry this
traffic are fully operational: wan_r0_r1 (router0 eth2 ↔ router1 eth2,
10.10.0.0/8) and wan_r1_r2 (router1 eth3 ↔ router2 eth2, 20.20.0.0/8) are
both reported UP/LOWER_UP with non-zero RX/TX counters showing live traffic
traversal. All three routers (router0, router1, router2) carry a fully
converged RIP routing table that includes the 128.168.0.0/16 prefix reachable
via the expected next hops. The 192.168.3.0/24 Office subnet is present on
router1 eth0 and is reachable from router2. There is no missing route, no
interface down state, and no forwarding black hole anywhere on the path. The
reported outage does not correspond to any observable fault in the current
network state. No corrective action is needed; the ticket should be closed as
a false alarm, and the reporting user should be asked to recheck connectivity
from their specific workstation as the issue may have been transient or
self-resolved before this investigation began.
=== END ===
